{"id":"6411e99d-bff7-4cd6-9c2b-bdbe13db659f","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The array of arguments is typically expected to be non-null when invoking main, as per Java specification.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.069961Z"}
{"id":"c7bcc159-6b8d-460a-bb6c-53025bc26efd","expr":"b == 0 || result == a / b","rationale":"If b is 0, we don't perform the division; otherwise, the result is a divided by b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.071086Z"}
{"id":"0f3dc8c0-33a4-461f-9eb2-648bd49f1eb8","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The parameter 'args' is an array reference provided for the main method and is never null when run from the command line.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.070032Z"}
{"id":"7ad6f8d5-b6eb-4451-a079-8be66ab1bb3f","expr":"b != 0 || result == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is 0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE as a designated 'error' value.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.071086Z"}
{"id":"9903909f-2758-4c6a-8aa2-717c878ec94e","expr":"b == 0 || b * (a / b) <= a && b * (a / b) >= (a - Math.abs(b) + 1)","rationale":"If b != 0, b * (a / b) provides the largest multiple of b less than or equal to a (for positive b), capturing properties of integer division.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.071310Z"}
{"id":"11449ba8-8417-47c2-8ccb-2a10f159e9aa","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length in Java is always non-negative, so this must hold for String[] args.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.069961Z"}
{"id":"50459389-f192-444f-a6c7-bcf092080b83","expr":"b == 0 || (a / b) * b + a % b == a","rationale":"For b != 0, the division and remainder relationship holds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.071310Z"}
{"id":"c3b9e188-88ea-426e-9923-5f9ca2ffc220","expr":"b == 0 || result * b == a - (a % b)","rationale":"If b is not 0, result equals a / b; thus, result * b is a - remainder.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.071086Z"}
{"id":"06ed624f-529d-4203-879a-1b333b3833d5","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"An array's length is always non-negative in Java.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.070032Z"}
{"id":"acec9535-e0da-4922-9841-fcde0fb8588d","expr":"b != 0 || result < 0","rationale":"When b is 0, the result is Integer.MIN_VALUE, which is a negative number.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.071086Z"}
{"id":"7a0ac922-c4e5-46f2-9f5c-5d9fd5fccdb9","expr":"b != Integer.MIN_VALUE || b != 0","rationale":"b can be Integer.MIN_VALUE or zero, but special care might be required in those extreme values.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.071310Z"}
{"id":"98c41eca-2e3b-497e-92ca-62413f48ce20","expr":"Math.abs(result) <= Math.abs(a)","rationale":"The absolute value of the quotient (when b != 0) or the special value is always less than or equal to |a|.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:09.071086Z"}
